# --- Site ---
# Canonical origin for metadata, robots, and the sitemap. Optional in development.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://errorwolf.dev

# --- PostHog (optional; omit both to run without PostHog) ---
# Use your own PostHog project when forking so events stay separate.

# Project token (`phc_...`). Vite inlines this into the browser bundle and the
# Worker bundle at build time. A project token is public by design.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Origin of the Cloudflare reverse proxy that fronts PostHog ingest. Both this
# and the token must be set, or the browser SDK stays off. Do not point it at
# us.i.posthog.com: the proxy is what keeps ingest on a first-party hostname
# that ad blockers do not match.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=

# --- Source maps (CI only) ---
# Personal API key (`phx_...`) with write access to error tracking, plus the
# environment id. `pnpm run sourcemaps:upload` needs both. Without them the
# build skips source maps and still succeeds.
# NEVER commit a real phx_ key. The repo is public.
# POSTHOG_CLI_API_KEY=
# POSTHOG_CLI_ENV_ID=

# --- Cloudflare Worker runtime (optional) ---
# Set these with `wrangler secret put` (or the `vars` block in wrangler.jsonc)
# to point the deployed Worker at another PostHog project without a rebuild.
# POSTHOG_KEY=
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
